<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεπί-πληκτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not liable to be reproved,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				397
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					922
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				489
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			, f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.454
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in bad sense,
				<i>not reproved, licentious,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροφῇ ἀ. τραφῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					695b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.Mynd.
				62
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not reproving</i> or <i>blaming,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ.</span>
			<i>abstinence from blam</i> or <i>criticism,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				1.10
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
